1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,360
10月23日傍晚，北方好几个省的人，
On the evening of October 23rd, people across northern China

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:06,380
同时看见天上飘过一只发光的大水母。
all saw a glowing jellyfish drift across the sky.

3
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:07,710
它不是外星人，
It wasn't aliens.

4
00:00:07,710 --> 00:00:08,970
是一枚火箭。
It was a rocket.

5
00:00:08,970 --> 00:00:11,200
今天的问题：太阳都下山了，
Today's question: the sun had already set,

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,560
火箭的尾巴为什么还会发光？
so why was the rocket's trail glowing?

7
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:14,850
认识一下小箭。
Meet Archie.

8
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:17,000
一枚刚出门上班的火箭。
A rocket heading off to work.

9
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,570
18点15分，长征六号改火箭
At 6:15 p.m., a Long March 6 rocket

10
00:00:19,570 --> 00:00:22,450
从山西的太原卫星发射中心起飞。
lifted off from the Taiyuan launch center in Shanxi.

11
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:24,340
它要把遥感五十号03星
Its job: carry the Yaogan-50 03 satellite

12
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:25,310
送上太空。
into space.

13
00:00:25,310 --> 00:00:26,830
这颗卫星的活儿，
The satellite's work:

14
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:29,990
是看国土、估产量、帮着防灾减灾。
surveying land, estimating crops, helping with disasters.

15
00:00:29,990 --> 00:00:31,660
这是长征系列火箭的
It was the Long March family's

16
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:33,270
第672次飞行。
672nd flight.

17
00:00:33,270 --> 00:00:36,110
那天傍晚，山西、河北、山东、河南，
That evening, in Shanxi, Hebei, Shandong and Henan,

18
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:38,400
好多人的朋友圈都被刷屏了。
social feeds were flooded.

19
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:39,650
有人说像水母，
Some said jellyfish.

20
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:41,720
有人说像一盏太空灯笼。
Some said a space lantern.

21
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:43,270
原因一：太阳下山，
Reason one: the sun sets

22
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:44,590
只是对你下山。
only for you.

23
00:00:44,590 --> 00:00:47,480
你站在地上，已经进了地球的影子；
On the ground, you're already in Earth's shadow.

24
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:49,950
可越往高处，太阳落得越晚。
But the higher you go, the later the sun sets.

25
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:51,330
就像傍晚的高楼：
Like a tall building at dusk:

26
00:00:51,330 --> 00:00:53,350
楼下黑了，楼顶还亮着。
dark at the bottom, still lit at the top.

27
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:55,190
火箭飞到上百公里高，
A rocket a hundred kilometers up

28
00:00:55,190 --> 00:00:56,790
那里还是大白天。
is still in broad daylight.

29
00:00:56,790 --> 00:01:00,700
我们粗算一下：那时太阳落到地平线下4度左右，
Our rough math: the sun was about 4 degrees below the horizon,

30
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:03,490
地球影子的顶，只有十几公里高。
so Earth's shadow only reached about 15 kilometers up.

31
00:01:03,490 --> 00:01:04,750
比这高的东西，
Anything higher than that

32
00:01:04,750 --> 00:01:06,490
全都还被太阳照着。
was still in sunshine.

33
00:01:06,490 --> 00:01:07,700
所以天是黑的，
So the sky was dark,

34
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:09,890
火箭的尾巴却被阳光点亮。
but the rocket's trail was lit by the sun.

35
00:01:09,890 --> 00:01:11,140
就像黑屋子里，
Like a dark room

36
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:13,410
一束光照亮了飘着的灰尘。
where a sunbeam lights up floating dust.

37
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:14,920
原因二，最反直觉：
Reason two, the weird one:

38
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:17,880
为什么是一只大水母，不是一条细线？
why a giant jellyfish, not a thin line?

39
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:19,840
在地面附近，空气很稠，
Near the ground, the air is thick.

40
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:22,630
尾焰被空气按住，只是细细一条。
It holds the exhaust into a narrow trail.

41
00:01:22,630 --> 00:01:24,420
可到了一百多公里高，
But a hundred-plus kilometers up,

42
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:26,510
空气稀得差不多是真空。
the air is so thin it's nearly a vacuum.

43
00:01:26,510 --> 00:01:27,770
没有空气按着，
With nothing holding it back,

44
00:01:27,770 --> 00:01:30,760
喷出来的气就往四面八方猛地散开。
the exhaust bursts out in every direction.

45
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,890
就像拧开一瓶摇过的汽水：
Like opening a shaken soda:

46
00:01:32,890 --> 00:01:34,600
气一下子全冲出来。
the gas rushes out all at once.

47
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:36,880
这一团气，能胀成好几公里宽。
That cloud can swell to several kilometers wide.

48
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:39,120
这是估算，要看当时的高度。
That's an estimate; it depends on the altitude.

49
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:41,990
气里的水汽一冷，就冻成小冰晶，
The water vapor freezes into tiny ice crystals

50
00:01:41,990 --> 00:01:43,640
把阳光散射出来。
that scatter the sunlight.

51
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:45,000
所以亮的不是火，
So the glow isn't fire.

52
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,820
是被太阳照亮的冰雾。
It's sunlit ice fog.

53
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:49,390
原因三：为什么好几个省都看得到？
Reason three: why could several provinces see it?

54
00:01:49,390 --> 00:01:50,640
因为它太高了。
Because it was so high.

55
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:52,270
站得越高，看得越远，
The higher something is, the farther it can be seen,

56
00:01:52,270 --> 00:01:54,030
这是因为地球是圆的。
because Earth is round.

57
00:01:54,030 --> 00:01:56,960
我们粗算一下：两百公里高的东西，
Our rough math: something 200 kilometers up

58
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:59,090
一千多公里外都看得见。
can be seen from over 1,000 kilometers away.

59
00:01:59,090 --> 00:02:00,400
从太原到大连，
From Taiyuan to Dalian

60
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:02,200
直线大约八百公里。
is about 800 kilometers in a straight line.

61
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,590
所以大连的网友，
So people in Dalian

62
00:02:03,590 --> 00:02:04,750
也拍到了它。
caught it on camera too.

63
00:02:04,750 --> 00:02:06,960
还得赶上刚刚好的时间：
And the timing has to be just right:

64
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:09,490
太早，天太亮，看不出来。
too early, and the sky is too bright.

65
00:02:09,490 --> 00:02:11,950
太晚，连高空也进了地球的影子。
Too late, and even the high sky falls into shadow.

66
00:02:11,950 --> 00:02:14,700
太原那天日落大约在17点58分。
Sunset in Taiyuan that day was around 5:58.

67
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:16,320
日落后一刻钟起飞，
Liftoff a quarter hour after sunset:

68
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:18,780
地上黑了，天上还亮，正好。
dark ground, bright sky. Perfect.

69
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:20,430
反转：同样的道理，
Plot twist: you see the same thing

70
00:02:20,430 --> 00:02:21,840
你其实天天见。
almost every day.

71
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:22,880
太阳下山后，
After sunset,

72
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:25,090
飞机拉的白线还亮一会儿。
a plane's contrail keeps glowing for a while.

73
00:02:25,090 --> 00:02:25,740
天黑了，
After dark,

74
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:27,810
远处的山顶还被照得金黄。
distant mountaintops still glow gold.

75
00:02:27,810 --> 00:02:29,470
天黑后一两个小时，
An hour or two after dark,

76
00:02:29,470 --> 00:02:33,100
你常能看到一颗亮点慢慢划过，那是卫星。
you can often spot a slow moving dot. That's a satellite.

77
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:34,510
它们都在高处，
They're all up high,

78
00:02:34,510 --> 00:02:36,040
还泡在阳光里。
still bathing in sunlight.

79
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:37,990
友情提示：火箭云很美，
Friendly fine print: rocket clouds are beautiful,

80
00:02:37,990 --> 00:02:40,400
可过一会儿，就慢慢散开了。
but they fade before long.

81
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,480
想看下一只？
Want to see the next one?

82
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:43,930
留意日落后不久的发射预告。
Watch for launches scheduled just after sunset.

83
00:02:43,930 --> 00:02:45,860
然后往发射场的方向看，
Then look toward the launch site,

84
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:47,730
离几百公里也没关系。
even from hundreds of kilometers away.

85
00:02:47,730 --> 00:02:49,220
小箭已经下班了，
Archie has clocked out.

86
00:02:49,220 --> 00:02:50,460
卫星送到了。
The satellite was delivered.

87
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:52,470
下次它再在傍晚出门，
Next time it heads out at dusk,

88
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:53,600
记得抬头。
look up.

89
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:56,190
那只发光水母，是高空在跟你说：
That glowing jellyfish is the sky telling you:

90
00:02:56,190 --> 00:02:58,440
我这儿，太阳还没落呢。
up here, the sun hasn't set yet.

